<h2>Carlsbad claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My new Carlsbad home was damaged in a storm, and the insurer says it was a construction defect. What can I do?</summary><div class="a"><p>An independent inspection can help separate storm damage from workmanship issues. If the dispute is about the amount of storm damage, appraisal can address it; if the carrier denies coverage based on a defect exclusion, consult a New Mexico attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can local contractor bids be used in appraisal?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. Appraisers consider actual market pricing, and documented local bids are relevant evidence of what repairs cost in the area.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is flooding from the Pecos River covered by homeowners insurance?</summary><div class="a"><p>Flood from rising water is generally excluded from standard homeowners policies. Coverage is available separately through the NFIP or private flood insurers.</p></div></details></div>
